From fdbaf47c12b13a92d0cb324f8bb6af9520e53069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuanLiz <47019693+JuanLiz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:07:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] btm_sec: complete a pending encryption procedure on the
 encryption change event

The incoming-CTKD hardening marks the link as encrypted before reading the
key size, so when the encryption change event finally arrives the record is
already flagged and the event was ignored. The device record then stayed in
BTM_SEC_STATE_ENCRYPTING and every later outgoing connection that needed
encryption (AVDTP, RFCOMM channels) waited forever in the security queue.
Only ignore the event when no local encryption procedure is pending.

Change-Id: I9cae689e6dccfea9902ab7a4d737cba31e851fac
---
 system/stack/btm/btm_sec.cc | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/system/stack/btm/btm_sec.cc b/system/stack/btm/btm_sec.cc
index 2d87034024..0c2576b880 100644
--- a/system/stack/btm/btm_sec.cc
+++ b/system/stack/btm/btm_sec.cc
@@ -3459,7 +3459,9 @@ void btm_sec_encrypt_change(uint16_t handle, tHCI_STATUS status,
     if (encr_enable) {
       if (p_dev_rec->hci_handle == handle) {  // classic
         if ((p_dev_rec->sec_flags & BTM_SEC_AUTHENTICATED) &&
-            (p_dev_rec->sec_flags & BTM_SEC_ENCRYPTED)) {
+            (p_dev_rec->sec_flags & BTM_SEC_ENCRYPTED) &&
+            p_dev_rec->sec_state != BTM_SEC_STATE_ENCRYPTING &&
+            p_dev_rec->sec_state != BTM_SEC_STATE_DELAY_FOR_ENC) {
           LOG_INFO(
               "Link is authenticated & encrypted, ignoring this enc change "
               "event");
-- 
